  "goodToKnow": "Der Vers is a line of a poem: ein Gedicht in Versen, gereimte Verse. A stanza or verse of a song is die Strophe, which often trips up English speakers. Bible verses are also Verse. The idiom sich keinen Vers auf etwas machen können means not to be able to make sense of something. The V is pronounced like an f: FERS. From Latin versus (turning, line). Plural: die Verse."
